  <!-- Getting Started -->
  <h2 id="getting-started">Getting Started with Email Marketing</h2>
  <p>
    Ready to start building your list? Here's a quick setup guide:
  </p>

  <h3>Step 1: Choose Your Platform</h3>
  <p>
    Based on our recommendations, pick a platform that matches your goals. For most creators, we recommend starting with
    ConvertKit or MailerLite—both have generous free tiers and room to grow.
  </p>

  <h3>Step 2: Create Your First Form</h3>
  <p>
    Set up an opt-in form to start collecting subscribers. Place it on your website, share it on social media, or create
    a standalone landing page. Offer something valuable in exchange for email addresses.
  </p>

  <h3>Step 3: Write Your Welcome Sequence</h3>
  <p>
    Create a 3-5 email welcome sequence that introduces you, delivers value, and sets expectations. This automation runs
    for every new subscriber and builds the relationship from day one.
  </p>

  <h3>Step 4: Establish a Consistent Schedule</h3>
  <p>
    Decide on a publishing cadence and stick to it. Weekly is a good starting point for most creators. Consistency
    matters more than frequency—your subscribers should know when to expect your emails.
  </p>

  <h3>Step 5: Monitor and Improve</h3>
  <p>
    Track your open rates, click rates, and unsubscribes. Healthy metrics are 30%+ open rates and under 0.5% unsubscribe
    rate. Test subject lines, sending times, and content types to improve over time.
  </p>

